{"text": "DANE COUNTY\nDISTRICT ATTORNEY\nISMAEL R. OZANNE\n\nAugust 28, 2019\n\nAttorney Jonas Bednarek\nHurley, Burish SC\n33 E Main St Ste 400\nMadison, WI 53703\n\nAttorney Marcus Berghan\nHurley, Burish SC\n33 E Main St Ste 400\nMadison, Wi 53703\n\nRE:\n\nDear Mr. Bednarek and Mr. Berghahn\n\n| am writing to inform you that Dr. Barbara L. Knox, MD, is currently on\nadministrative leave from her position in the University of Wisconsin School of Medicine\nand Public Health's Department of Pediatrics. My understanding is that the university is\ninvestigating concerns that Dr. Knox does not timely complete work and also complaints\nabout her behavior with internal and external colleagues, but nothing that would rise to\nthe level of criminal or harassing behavior. | have been in contact with the University of\n\u2018Wisconsin-Madison Office of Legal Affairs as well as the Department of Pediatrics. |\nhave asked both entities to alert me if they become aware of any issues related to\ndishonesty or to incorrect medical diagnoses.\n\nSincerely,\nWlatthew Wloceer\n\nMatthew D. Moeser\nDeputy District Attorney\n\nDane County Courthouse 215 S. Hamilton Street Room 3000 Madison WI 53703-3297\nPh (608) 266-4211 Fax (608) 267-2545 http:/ww.co dane wius/daofficeldahome.htm",
